   "date": "2017-02-04T20:54:59Z",
   "subject": "Re: ggplot2 stacked bar chart unsorted stacks",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thank you very much for answering Roman.<div><br></div><div>It does seem to give the same results as the example</div><div>Although it&#39;s not quite what I&#39;m looking for.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve made a new example to better illustrate what I&#39;m looking for.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">c </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Monday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Monday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Monday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Monday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Monday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Tuesday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Tuesday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Tuesday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Tuesday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Tuesday&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></font><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">colnames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Day&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Time&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;State&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Day</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Time</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">State</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;identity&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div>What I&#39;m looking for is to plot a stacked bar plot where the y axis represents time from 0 to 24 hours.</div><div>Each entry in the dataframe describes if the system was active or inactive (true / false) during that period.</div><div>I&#39;d like this to be illustrated with one color for each state, but it&#39;s very important that no grouping / reordering of the data occurs.</div><div><br></div><div>Is this possible to achieve with ggplot? If so, do you know how?</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mOjWsZJUBwAJ",
   "from": "hst...@gmail.com",
   "author": "323ad97114428ea0",
   "date": "2017-02-04T21:23:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: ggplot2 stacked bar chart unsorted stacks",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Roman,<div><br></div><div>You were entirely correct.</div><div>The desired functionality only meant that I had to group on a parameter that was the same for the whole stack.</div><div>In my second example that would be the &quot;Day&quot;</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div>ggplot(data=c, aes(x=Day, y=Time, fill=State, group=Day)) + <span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">geom_bar(stat=&quot;identity&quot;)</span></div></div></code></div><br>Thanks for the help!</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
